From: Ivan D Vasin <ivan@nisavid.io>
Subject: [PATCH] Require protected first-admin bootstrap and an administrator at startup
X-Open-WebUI-Commit: 8bd8b4fac5e059578ac0c74b3c18d11139f88b7d
X-Open-WebUI-Sdist-SHA256: 1f1a31668a0dee733953c29d6183d78dd78984e696aa8eb0f2083f5796497be0

An empty restored database must not reopen remote first-administrator signup.
Require an administrator before startup completes, and gate the shared auth
insertion seam before it stages either row. Only credential-driven startup may
opt into initial admin creation; existing users forbid that opt-in. Normal
commissioned restarts and later household user creation remain unchanged.

Apply after 0006: its authentication utility changes are disjoint from this
patch's startup-only creation call. No database schema or migration changes.

diff --git a/backend/open_webui/models/auths.py b/backend/open_webui/models/auths.py
--- a/backend/open_webui/models/auths.py
+++ b/backend/open_webui/models/auths.py
@@ -110,9 +110,20 @@
         role: str = 'pending',
         oauth: dict | None = None,
         db: AsyncSession | None = None,
+        *,
+        initial_admin: bool = False,
     ) -> UserModel | None:
         """Create an Auth + User pair inside a single transaction."""
         async with get_async_db_context(db) as session:
+            # Only credential-driven startup may create the first administrator.
+            # HTTP, LDAP, trusted-header, and OAuth callers all use this seam.
+            # Check before staging either row so denial has no write side effects.
+            if initial_admin:
+                if role != 'admin' or await Users.has_users(db=session):
+                    return None
+            elif await Users.get_super_admin_user(db=session) is None:
+                return None
+
             log.info('insert_new_auth')
 
             new_id = str(uuid.uuid4())
diff --git a/backend/open_webui/utils/auth.py b/backend/open_webui/utils/auth.py
--- a/backend/open_webui/utils/auth.py
+++ b/backend/open_webui/utils/auth.py
@@ -653,6 +653,7 @@
             password=hashed,
             name=name,
             role='admin',
+            initial_admin=True,
         )
         if user:
             log.info('Admin account created successfully: %s', email)
diff --git a/backend/open_webui/main.py b/backend/open_webui/main.py
--- a/backend/open_webui/main.py
+++ b/backend/open_webui/main.py
@@ -379,6 +379,14 @@
             # Disable signup since we now have an admin
             await Config.upsert({'ui.enable_signup': False})
 
+    # Refuse service readiness after database loss or an incomplete restore.
+    # A failed credential bootstrap must not expose first-user registration.
+    if await Users.get_super_admin_user() is None:
+        raise RuntimeError(
+            'Open WebUI requires an administrator: restore a commissioned database '
+            'or commission with protected credentials while the route is closed'
+        )
+
     if SAFE_MODE:
         await Functions.deactivate_all_functions()
 
